   "subject": "New paper using Stan",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hello,<div><br></div><div>My colleagues and I have just published a new paper using Stan. We were interested in modelling the variability of sex differences in cancer incidence over time, age, and region. Stan was the obvious choice to fit these hierarchical, overdispersed Poisson models.</div><div><br></div><div>\n\t\n\t\n\t\n\n\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:135%\">Scelo G., Li P.,\nChanudet E., Muller D.C. 2017. Variability of Sex Disparities in\nCancer Incidence over 30 Years: The Striking Case of Kidney Cancer.\n<i>European Urology Focus</i>. doi:10.1016/j.euf.2017.01.006</p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:135%\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:135%\">I&#39;ll submit a pull request to add this to the citations page on the Stan website.</p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:135%\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:135%\">David</p></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
