   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi Andrew,<div><br></div><div>I&#39;d forgotten about that example in BDA, but will revisit it. You&#39;re right, Kidney cancer rates themselves are highly variable across time and region (this is interesting per se, as it&#39;s a combination of real differences/changes and changes in coding and registration). On the other hand, despite this massive variability in rates, men have 2-fold higher incidence than women, almost uniformly!</div><div><br></div><div>David</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
